\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesu, Thy blood and righteousness
\par My beauty are, my glorious dress;
\par Midst flaming worlds, in these arrayed,
\par With joy shall I lift up my head.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Bold shall I stand in Thy great day;
\par For who aught to my charge shall lay?
\par Fully absolved through these I am,
\par From sin and fear, from guilt and shame.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The holy, meek, unspotted Lamb,
\par Who from the Father's bosom came,
\par Who died for me, even me, to atone,
\par Now for my Lord and God I own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord, I believe Thy precious blood,
\par Which at the mercy-seat of God
\par For ever doth for sinners plead,
\par For me, even for my soul, was shed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. When from the dust of death I rise
\par To claim my mansion in the skies,
\par Even then this shall  be all my  plea-
\par Jesus hath lived, hath died for me!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Jesu, be endless praise to Thee,
\par Whose boundless mercy hath for me,
\par For me and all Thy hands have made,
\par An everlasting ransom paid.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Lord, I believe, were sinners more
\par Than sands upon the ocean shore,
\par Thou hast for all a ransom paid,
\par For all a full atonement made.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Ah! give to all Thy servants, Lord,
\par With power to speak Thy gracious word,
\par That all who to Thy wounds will flee,
\par May find eternal life in Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9. Thou God of power, Thou God of love,
\par Let the whole world Thy mercy prove!
\par Now let Thy world Thy mercy prove!
\par Now take the spoils of death and hell.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10. O let the dead now hear Thy voice,
\par Now bid Thy banished ones rejoice,
\par Their beauty this, their glorious dress,
\par Jesu, Thy blood and righteousness!
\par 
\par \f1 
